James sought suggestions to shorten the title of his paper about comprehensive assessments of national climate damages, initially titled "Towards comprehensive assessments of national climate damages: an application to the United Kingdom," to fit within 90 characters without punctuation. After receiving initial suggestions that were shorter than intended, he clarified that while he didn't want to emphasize the UK too heavily, he was open to including it in some way. Arachne then provided revised titles that incorporated a British context while maintaining a methodological focus, such as "Towards Comprehensive Assessments of National Climate Damages A Methodology for the UK."
